    {
      "id": "p0250-b013",
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "source": {
        "text": "Toby and the localization team spent a lot of time on preserving this wordplay in Japanese. After trying a number of solutions, the team settled on using the Japanese wordfukkatsu in place of\"save\". In general,fukkatsu means \"to revive\" or \"to restore\", but it can also be used to mean \"to restore/load a saved file\" and \"to restore something back to how it should be\".",
        "raw": "Toby and the localization team spent a lot of time on preserving this wordplay\nin Japanese. After trying a number of solutions, the team settled on using\nthe Japanese wordfukkatsu in place of\"save\". In general,fukkatsu means \"to\nrevive\" or \"to restore\", but it can also be used to mean \"to restore/load a saved\nfile\" and \"to restore something back to how it should be\".",
        "status": "corrected",
        "languages": [
          "en"
        ],
        "bbox": [
          0.290805,
          0.69512857,
          0.88727247,
          0.78061429
        ],
        "mask_bbox": [
          0.28651822,
